#: ../../architecture.rst:2 33345cc6966c4ccea6c571f7620632fb
msgid "Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:4 d5416fe2105e4f2498cefc10e5164b7a
msgid ""
"A single FastAPI app (``api/main.py``) assembling routers grouped by "
"access level:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:7 2cc823fae1c54916befb89d317c274f5
msgid "``api/routes/health.py`` -- public."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:8 ddc3cd2e458f4fb4a25fbf9ffee6d0bb
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``api/routes/metrics.py`` -- public (matches ``health.py``, and how "
"Prometheus is configured to scrape it -- no bearer token). ``GET "
"/metrics`` computes a fresh Prometheus exposition on every scrape from "
"each registered script's last recorded run (Redis, via "
"``api/run_store.py``): every numeric key in ``ScriptResult.metrics`` as "
"``rewake_api_script_metric{script, metric}``, plus "
"``rewake_api_script_duration_seconds``, "
"``rewake_api_script_last_run_success`` (0/1), and "
"``rewake_api_script_last_run_timestamp_seconds``. Computed fresh rather "
"than accumulated in-process because scripts actually run in the Celery "
"worker/beat processes, not this one -- an in-process Counter/Gauge here "
"would never observe their updates. Scraped by RewakeObserve's Prometheus "
"(``prometheus/prometheus.yml``, job ``rewake-api``); the two dashboards "
"under its ``grafana/provisioning/dashboards/`` query these series."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:23 0fddefcddc14420d8688ac2768b7ace5
msgid ""
"``api/routes/hellopro/``, ``api/routes/machinio/`` -- external "
"integrations, each gated by its own static token (no origin check)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:25 480b47ea45f34d93aa2bcc77ef2c502f
msgid ""
"``api/routes/internal/`` -- the internal surface used by "
"``app.rewake.fr``/ ``sav.rewake.fr``, gated by ``APP_TOKEN`` **and** an "
"allowed origin/referer (``ADMIN_TOKEN`` bypasses the origin check "
"everywhere; ``scripts.py`` also accepts ``AIRTABLE_AUTOMATION_TOKEN``) --"
" see :doc:`authentication`. Besides the older "
"contact/affaire/fees/formulaire/pdf/model routes, it holds ``catalog/`` "
"(receiving workflow and commercial review, see :doc:`catalog_intake`), "
"``ai/`` (settings and usage of the central AI service) and ``scripts.py``"
" (below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:33 060a5b8090434af3bde1c116aa539565
msgid ""
"``api/routes/invoice/``, ``api/routes/pdf/``, ``api/routes/formulaire/`` "
"-- public, token-less ``GET`` routes serving files written by internal "
"routes (saved invoices, generated PDFs, form photos); see :doc:`routes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:37 2f344b709e0e4200b67a0d4c0bcd1bb0
msgid ""
"``api/services/`` holds the business and integration logic, reused across"
" routes rather than duplicated in them: ``airtable.py`` (Airtable REST + "
"caches), ``fees.py``, ``gmail.py``, ``pdf.py``, ``parsers/`` (invoice "
"parsing), and the catalog services -- ``catalog_sync.py``, "
"``catalog_lookup.py``, ``catalog_index.py``, ``catalog_reprise.py``, "
"``unit_photos.py``, ``label_ocr.py``, ``reference_suggestion.py``, "
"``product_research.py``, ``product_assist.py``, ``review_queue.py``, "
"``model_sheet.py`` -- and ``ai/`` (the central AI service: Anthropic and "
"OpenRouter providers, settings, pricing, usage store in SQLite). "
"``api/integrations/`` holds the Shopify clients (``shopify.py`` GraphQL, "
"``shopify_rest.py``, ``shopify_files.py``, ``shopify_auth.py``), "
"``api/domain/`` the catalog/intake dataclasses. ``api/utils/`` holds "
"cross-cutting concerns: ``auth.py`` (the token/origin dependency), "
"``logger.py`` (structlog setup + request logging middleware), "
"``token.py``, ``pdf.py``, ``pdf_compression.py``. The ``ocr/`` directory "
"is a separate RapidOCR HTTP service (its own image), called by the worker"
" for label OCR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:55 4981f079ec3e46b2a4d4d87037249f98
msgid "Scripts: a registry, not one-off endpoints"
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:57 e48a6c3c421b40f485783dd289758b20
msgid ""
"``api/routes/internal/scripts.py``'s ``POST /internal/scripts/update`` "
"and ``POST /internal/scripts/verification`` were the only scripted "
"automation in this API, and turned out to have no real caller: "
"``app.rewake.fr`` runs its own equivalents by shelling out directly from "
"Next.js (``app/api/lauch_script/*``), bypassing this API entirely. With "
"nothing depending on their exact shape, they've been replaced outright by"
" the registry pattern described below rather than kept alongside a new "
"parallel implementation. ``verification_shopify`` (a thin wrapper around "
"the sibling ``Verification-Shopify-Airtable`` project, itself an older, "
"separate Airtable/Shopify comparison) was ported alongside them briefly, "
"then removed outright once ``shopify_catalog_reconciliation`` below "
"covered the same comparison properly -- there was no reason to keep two "
"ways to check the same thing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:71 f11ce5ed97ff4553ae98a4b664975ab6
msgid ""
"``api/scripts/base.py`` -- ``ApiScript`` (a ``name``, an optional "
"``schedule``, and a ``run(previous_snapshot=None, **kwargs) -> "
"(ScriptResult, new_snapshot | None)``) and ``ScriptResult`` (status, "
"details, metrics, duration). ``schedule`` is ``None`` for purely on-"
"demand scripts -- a script with a real schedule is still also runnable on"
" demand, through the exact same endpoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:77 697821a6f4b542f9ac51933ad8f3fa78
msgid ""
"``api/scripts/update_product.py`` -- on-demand only (``schedule = "
"None``), ported in-process from a subprocess call against a sibling "
"``Update-Product`` project (see :doc:`update_product` for the full story,"
" including deliberate deviations from that project). Takes either a "
"Variation ``record_id`` (default) or a Model ``model_id`` -- both "
"converge on the same update, since Shopify variants all belong to one "
"product per Model. Shares its exception class, Airtable cache, link "
"builders, and unit/spec aggregation with ``create_product_shopify.py`` "
"via ``api/scripts/_shopify_links.py``, rather than duplicating them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:86 ce8c7b4919cc48e58797384edb98ee87
msgid ""
"``api/scripts/create_product_shopify.py`` -- on-demand only, creates a "
"new Shopify listing from an Airtable Model (see "
":doc:`create_product_shopify` for the full story, including deliberate "
"deviations from the Cloud Function it was ported from). Native code, not "
"a subprocess wrapper -- the other script here that writes to Shopify, "
"alongside ``update_product`` (which only ever updates a listing that "
"already exists)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:92 fca2b57ee8294a41a3d412a5339aef64
msgid ""
"``api/scripts/shopify_catalog_reconciliation.py``, "
"``api/scripts/airtable_catalog_stats.py`` -- this business logic was "
"developed and validated against real production data (two genuine "
"Airtable/Shopify matching bugs found and fixed along the way -- see "
"``docs/shopify_catalog_reconciliation.md``). Scheduled (hourly / daily-"
"at-20:42-Europe/Paris) via a real ``schedule``, and read via "
"``api/domain/catalog.py`` (the Model/Variation/Unit/ShopifyListing "
"dataclasses, built on this project's own existing "
"``api/services/airtable`` functions rather than a separate client class) "
"and ``api/integrations/shopify.py`` (the Shopify GraphQL client, using "
"``requests`` to match what this project already uses everywhere else)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:103 9efa49dc46c648bbad5939c638c04a55
msgid ""
"``api/scripts/registry.py`` -- ``SCRIPTS: dict[str, ApiScript]``. Adding "
"a script means adding one entry here; nothing else changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:105 78381260f4ec448eb10a0635dd0bdbba
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``api/tasks.py`` -- **one** generic Celery task for scripts, "
"``run_script(name, **kwargs)``, used for every script regardless of on-"
"demand vs. scheduled (the same module also holds the catalog's own tasks:"
" ``run_label_ocr``, ``run_product_research``, ``run_document_search``, "
"polled through ``/internal/catalog/*/{job_id}``). ``run_script`` it "
"checks ``is_configured()`` (recording a ``skipped`` result if credentials"
" are missing, rather than failing), fetches the previous snapshot from "
"Redis, runs the script, records the result, and persists the new snapshot"
" if one was returned. While it runs, the script reports its current stage"
" (``report_stage``), readable through ``GET "
"/internal/scripts/{name}/current`` and recorded as ``failed_at_stage`` on"
" failure. Retries automatically on any exception "
"(``autoretry_for=(Exception,)``, up to 3 times with backoff -- every "
"script here is network-call-heavy, where transient failures are the "
"expected failure mode)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:120 5fc2155f495f4f038ae8fe11b70d8be3
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Celery itself doesn't deduplicate concurrent invocations with the same "
"arguments -- nothing stops two ``POST /internal/scripts/{name}/run`` "
"calls for the *same* ``record_id`` from executing at the same time. "
"``run_script`` guards against this explicitly: when ``record_id`` is "
"present, it takes a Redis lock (``RunStore.acquire_lock``, ``SET NX`` "
"with a TTL as a crash safety net) before calling ``script.run(...)``, and"
" records a ``skipped`` result immediately (never calling ``run()`` at "
"all) if another run for that same ``record_id`` is already holding it -- "
"unless the script sets ``requeue_when_locked`` (``update_product``), in "
"which case the run is put back on the queue every 5 s (up to 120 times) "
"instead, since it may carry newer data. This is what actually stops "
"``create_product_shopify`` from creating two Shopify products for one "
"Model when triggered twice in quick succession -- a script's own "
"idempotence check alone only catches *sequential* retries (one finishes, "
"then a second one starts), not truly concurrent ones. Verified live: two "
"simultaneous triggers for the same record, one rejected in 5ms, the other"
" ran normally. ``update_product.py`` adds a *second* lock of its own, "
"inside ``run()``, keyed by the resolved Model id rather than whatever "
"Airtable id the caller passed in -- a Variation and its own Model (or two"
" sibling Variations) are different ``record_id``/``model_id`` values but "
"the same underlying Shopify product, which the outer per-``record_id`` "
"lock alone wouldn't catch. A run finding it held raises ``RequeueLater`` "
"and is requeued the same way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:143 9f0d332a4d424544ad81c7a309127b45
msgid ""
"``api/run_store.py`` -- a small Redis-backed history (last "
"``MAX_RUNS_PER_SCRIPT`` runs per script -- currently 1000, a deliberate "
"cap enforced with ``LTRIM`` on every write, not a Redis engineering "
"limit; older runs past it are gone, not just unpaginated-to) plus a per-"
"script snapshot slot, so a run's outcome is still inspectable after the "
"task itself has been garbage-collected from Celery's result backend, and "
"a scheduled script's day-over-day diff survives a worker/beat restart; "
"also the per-record_id lock described above and each running script's "
"current stage. ``RunStore.recent(script, limit, offset)`` pages through "
"this history via Redis ``LRANGE`` (cheap at arbitrary offsets for a list "
"this size), and ``RunStore.count(script)`` (``LLEN``) gives the frontend "
"a total so it knows when it's fetched everything. Each run's stored JSON "
"is small (a few KB, even for ``shopify_catalog_reconciliation``'s now-"
"uncapped ~300-entry missing-model lists), so 1000 of them per script is a"
" negligible amount of Redis memory -- raise ``MAX_RUNS_PER_SCRIPT`` "
"freely if more history is ever wanted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:161 5cf41fa1471342b8b5fa3a6eaf170eb6
msgid ""
"Endpoints, generic over the registry (unchanged by adding the two "
"scheduled scripts -- this is exactly the point of the registry):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:164 54832e5a455d42528f71b5f581066a87
msgid "``GET /internal/scripts/`` -- list registered script names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:165 6c8211785fd8468db1ed8d37cba5134f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``POST /internal/scripts/{name}/run`` -- queue a run (``record_id`` as a "
"query param for ``create_product_shopify``, or either ``record_id`` or "
"``model_id`` -- exactly one -- for ``update_product``); returns a "
"``task_id`` immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:169 7a55c6a912354889a2a9cf277ad7e105
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``GET /internal/scripts/status/{task_id}`` -- poll one task "
"(``PENDING``/``STARTED``/``RETRY``/``SUCCESS``/``FAILURE``, plus the "
"result once ready)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:172 4b9cc294d4104ed085d49907659f791c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``GET /internal/scripts/{name}/runs`` -- a page of that script's run "
"history (``limit``, default 20, max 100 per request; ``offset`` to page "
"further back), newest first, plus ``total`` (how many runs are stored in "
"total) so the frontend knows when it's reached the end. The RewakeApp "
"dashboard uses this for infinite scroll on the run history table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:177 225e26b22b1845d18129c5ed399cfd65
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``GET /internal/scripts/{name}/current`` -- the live stage of every in-"
"progress run of that script (one per ``record_id`` running at once), "
"empty when nothing runs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:181 b4d9837461364c0385fa537309eb7415
msgid ""
"A dedicated ``celery -A api.celery_app worker``/``beat`` process only "
"ever imports ``api/celery_app.py`` directly -- it never goes through "
"``api/main.py``, so it never imports ``api/tasks.py`` on its own. "
"``celery_app.py`` calls ``celery_app.autodiscover_tasks([\"api\"])`` for "
"exactly this reason; without it the worker starts with an empty task "
"registry and every dispatched task fails with ``NotRegistered`` (caught "
"by testing this end-to-end against a real worker before relying on it, "
"not just by reading the code -- same for the two new scheduled scripts' "
"``beat_schedule`` entries and their Redis snapshot round-trip, both "
"verified against the real, live Airtable/Shopify data before calling this"
" done)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:193 3b37a5cd6df245e28cc19f244710d79b
msgid ""
"``docker-compose.yml`` runs a ``redis`` service, a ``worker`` service "
"(``celery -A api.celery_app worker``), a ``beat`` service (``celery -A "
"api.celery_app beat``, needed once any script has a real ``schedule``) "
"and the ``ocr`` sidecar alongside the ``api`` service. This is the same "
"shape as the pattern planned for the rest of Rewake's automation: a "
"script behind a queue instead of Google Cloud Run or a bare subprocess "
"call, with a registry so adding one never means adding infrastructure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:203 64fedeec90904f1db1f92a80d5243eae
msgid "What's deliberately *not* duplicated here"
msgstr ""

#: ../../architecture.rst:205 89e4edca0c0a4c5bafecf70d761856ec
msgid ""
"Grafana/Prometheus/Loki/Uptime Kuma/Flower are planned as **one shared "
"stack** for all of Rewake's services, not one per project. This "
"repository's ``docker-compose.yml`` only adds what the API itself needs "
"to function (Redis, a worker, beat, OCR) -- it does not stand up its own "
"copy of that observability stack."
msgstr ""

